#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:10
msgid "Important Rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:12
msgid ""
"**Don't assume.** Surface tradeoffs and ask questions if anything is "
"unclear. Present multiple interpretations instead of picking one "
"silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:13
msgid ""
"**Honest over agreeable.** Push back when you disagree — say what's "
"wrong, propose the better path, then proceed. Don't reverse your position"
" because the user pushed; reverse it when new evidence warrants it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:14
msgid ""
"**Label what you know vs. think.** State facts as facts and opinions as "
"opinions. \"I'm not sure\" beats a confident guess."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:15
msgid ""
"**Say the hard thing.** If the user's approach has a flaw, point it out "
"before implementing. If a request conflicts with these rules, name the "
"conflict rather than silently following."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:16
msgid ""
"**Simplicity first.** Write the minimum code that solves the problem. No "
"speculative features, no unnecessary abstractions, and no error handling "
"for impossible scenarios."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:17
msgid ""
"**Surgical changes.** Touch only what is strictly required. Do not "
"\"improve\" nearby code or refactor unrelated sections. Match the "
"existing style perfectly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:18
msgid ""
"**Verify before reporting done.** Define clear success criteria for every"
" task. Run tests or validation scripts and iterate until the criteria are"
" met before reporting completion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:19
msgid ""
"**Local specs first.** When asked to work on bugs, features, or any "
"tracked items, ALWAYS check what's already imported locally before "
"querying the tracker. Use `hero search --list --type <type>` to find "
"local specs. Only go to the tracker if the local search comes up empty. "
"When working on multiple items (e.g. \"diagnose 10 bugs\"), select from "
"locally imported specs — never bulk-query the tracker to pick work items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:20
msgid ""
"Always check spec status before doing work — don't investigate closed "
"bugs or deliver completed specs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:21
msgid ""
"When a tracker is configured, sync status with `hero sync pull` before "
"starting work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:22
msgid ""
"**Hero handoff travels with commits.** When committing, stage any "
"modified `.hero/NEXT.md` and `.hero/next/*.md` alongside your code "
"changes. These are projected handoff files — if they don't travel with "
"the commit, the next session (possibly on another machine) starts cold. "
"`hero next install-hooks` installs a pre-commit hook that automates this;"
" the rule is your backstop when the hook isn't installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:23
msgid ""
"Capture novel learnings to `.hero/knowledge/` at the end of major "
"workflows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:24
msgid ""
"Specs use YAML frontmatter with fields: title, type, status, tracker_id, "
"priority, severity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.hero/knowledge/rules/project-rules/spec.md:25
msgid ""
"Imported specs include tracker-prefixed fields (e.g. jira_status, "
"jira_priority, jira_assignee) under a # Jira/GitHub/Linear comment header"
msgstr ""

